m/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T17:12:44-08:00","id":1526541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525971-icons-of-rage-available-for-backers?p=1526525#post1526525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't realize nobody did Evan until I got my copy but it was because nobody wanted to do Evan. Is funny that he us name dropped several times however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I found it odd when I looked at the table of contents and saw Albrecht and Mari Cabrah right off but didn't see Evan. Being a Philodox mediator between the tribes is what drew me to Evan's character (because that sort of unity is exactly what the Garou Nation needs in the End Times), but I can totally understand why people would get offended at the Mighty Whitey trope Evan represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T14:19:15-08:00","id":1526774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525971-icons-of-rage-available-for-backers?p=1526541#post1526541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I found it odd when I looked at the table of contents and saw Albrecht and Mari Cabrah right off but didn't see Evan. Being a Philodox mediator between the tribes is what drew me to Evan's character (because that sort of unity is exactly what the Garou Nation needs in the End Times), but I can totally understand why people would get offended at the Mighty Whitey trope Evan represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that there are books where the intro fiction has Evan show up to a Younger Brother Sept and tell the members, &quot;I know you're still pissed off about colonialism, but we have to focus on the Apocalypse.&quot; We've <i>all</i> had to deal with that one leftist who says that your material concerns are nothing compared to The Final Blow Against Capitalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d"